  "excerpt": "Our signature blend and about 55% of everything we roast. If a customer only ever buys one bag from us, it is this one. Recipe: 60% Colombia Huila (washed), 30% Brazil Cerrado (natural), 10% Ethiopia Guji (washed). Medium roast, dropped at 410°F, 16% shrinkage. Tastes like milk chocolate, toasted almond, dried cherry on the finish. Built to hold up in milk without disappearing. Why it works commercially: the Colombia and Brazil are volume lots with stable pricing from Supplier Directory, so the blend cost stays predictable even when specialty prices spike. The 10% Ethiopia is the aroma and the story — it is also the component most at risk when the lot in Green Bean Inventory runs low. It is…",
